.\" DO NOT MODIFY THIS FILE!  It was generated by help2man 1.49.3.
.TH SMBIOS-WIRELESS-CTL "1" "December 2025" "smbios-wireless-ctl 2.4.3" "User Commands"
.SH "نام (NAME)"
smbios-wireless-ctl \- ../src/bin/smbios-wireless-ctl
.SH "خلاصه دستور (SYNOPSIS)"
.B smbios-wireless-ctl

.SH "گزینه‌ها (OPTIONS)"
.TP
\fB\-\-version\fR
show program's version number and exit
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
show this help message and exit
.TP
\fB\-\-info\fR
Show wireless configuration (default)
.TP
\fB\-\-boot\fR
Set BIOS boot\-time setting.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-boot\fR
Do not set BIOS boot\-time setting.
.TP
\fB\-\-runtime\fR
Set BIOS runtime setting (default).
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-runtime\fR, \fB\-\-boot\-only\fR, \fB\-\-boot_only\fR
Do not set BIOS runtime setting.
.TP
\fB\-\-wlan\fR=\fI\,WLAN\/\fR
Set radio runtime status for wireless LAN
.TP
\fB\-\-bt\fR=\fI\,BT\/\fR
Set radio runtime status for Bluetooth
.TP
\fB\-\-wwan\fR=\fI\,WWAN\/\fR
Set radio runtime status for cellular (wireless WAN)
.TP
\fB\-\-uwb\fR=\fI\,UWB\/\fR
Set radio runtime status for UWB
.TP
\fB\-\-wigig\fR=\fI\,WIGIG\/\fR
Set radio runtime status for WiGig
.TP
\fB\-\-sw_wlan\fR=\fI\,SW_WLAN\/\fR
Set hardware switch so that it controls radio for
wireless LAN
.TP
\fB\-\-sw_bt\fR=\fI\,SW_BT\/\fR
Set hardware switch so that it controls radio for
Bluetooth
.TP
\fB\-\-sw_wwan\fR=\fI\,SW_WWAN\/\fR
Set hardware switch so that it controls radio for
cellular (wireless WAN)
.TP
\fB\-\-sw_uwb\fR=\fI\,SW_UWB\/\fR
Set hardware switch so that it controls radio for UWB
.TP
\fB\-\-sw_wigig\fR=\fI\,SW_WIGIG\/\fR
Set hardware switch so that it controls radio for
WiGig
.TP
\fB\-\-sw_locator\fR=\fI\,SW_LOCATOR\/\fR
Enable or disable the WIFI locator switch
.TP
\fB\-\-st_wlan\fR
Get status for wireless LAN. 0 = enabled. 1 =
disabled. 2 = not present. 3 = unsupported. 4 =
unknown.
.TP
\fB\-\-st_bt\fR
Get status for Bluetooth. 0 = enabled. 1 = disabled. 2
= not present. 3 = unsupported. 4 = unknown.
.TP
\fB\-\-st_wwan\fR
Get status for cellular (wireless WAN). 0 = enabled. 1
= disabled. 2 = not present. 3 = unsupported. 4 =
unknown.
.TP
\fB\-\-st_uwb\fR
Get status for UWB. 0 = enabled. 1 = disabled. 2 = not
present. 3 = unsupported. 4 = unknown.
.TP
\fB\-\-st_wigig\fR
Get status for WiGig. 0 = enabled. 1 = disabled. 2 =
not present. 3 = unsupported. 4 = unknown.
.TP
\fB\-\-st_locator\fR=\fI\,ST_LOCATOR\/\fR
Get status for locator switch
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Display more verbose output.
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Minimize program output. Only errors and warnings are
displayed.
.TP
\fB\-\-trace\fR
Enable verbose function tracing.
.TP
\fB\-\-logconfig\fR=\fI\,LOGCONFIG\/\fR
Specify alternate config log.
.TP
\fB\-\-security\-key\fR=\fI\,SECURITY_KEY\/\fR
BIOS pre\-calculated security key.
.TP
\fB\-\-password\fR=\fI\,PASSWORD\/\fR
BIOS Setup password for set/activate operations.
.TP
\fB\-r\fR, \fB\-\-rawpassword\fR
Do not auto\-convert password to scancodes.
.TP
\fB\-\-memory\-dat\fR=\fI\,MEMORY_DAT\/\fR
Path to a memory dump file to use instead of real RAM
.TP
\fB\-\-cmos\-dat\fR=\fI\,CMOS_DAT\/\fR
Path to a CMOS dump file to use instead of real CMOS
.SH "همچنین ببینید (SEE ALSO)"
The full documentation for
.B smbios-wireless-ctl
is maintained as a Texinfo manual.  If the
.B info
and
.B smbios-wireless-ctl
programs are properly installed at your site, the command
.IP
.B info smbios-wireless-ctl
.PP
should give you access to the complete manual.
